              ],
              "content": "(a)"
            },
            {
              "bbox": [
                0.131,
                0.397,
                0.504,
                0.415
              ],
              "content": "Fig. 8.15: (a) Heating Sample A; (b) Black mass"
            }
          ],
          "footnotes": [],
          "image_source": "images/page_10_image_6.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "bbox": [
            0.371,
            0.216,
            0.571,
            0.355
          ],
          "content": "",
          "captions": [
            {
              "bbox": [
                0.458,
                0.372,
                0.486,
                0.389
              ],
              "content": "(b)"
            }
          ],
          "footnotes": [],
          "image_source": "images/page_10_image_9.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.582,
            0.192,
            0.883,
            0.285
          ],
          "content": "Take half of Sample A in a china dish and gently heat it (Fig. 8.15a) with continuous stirring until a black mass is formed."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.583,
            0.287,
            0.882,
            0.324
          ],
          "content": "Let the content of the china dish cool."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.583,
            0.327,
            0.883,
            0.383
          ],
          "content": "Place this black mass in a mortar and grind it with the help of a pestle."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.583,
            0.384,
            0.883,
            0.441
          ],
          "content": "Now, put it on another watch glass and label it as Sample B (Fig. 8.15b)."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.272,
            0.441,
            0.884,
            0.499
          ],
          "content": "z Now, you have two samples— Sample A and Sample B (Fig. 8.16a and 8.16b). **Compare** both the Samples A and B step by step and **record** your observations in Table 8.2."
        },
